## Original Content
China and India will hold the 25th round of talks between their special representatives on the boundary question in Beijing on Tuesday, the Chinese Foreign Ministry announced on Monday.

## Summary
China and India will hold the 25th round of talks between their special representatives on the boundary question in Beijing. The meeting is scheduled for Tuesday and was announced by the Chinese Foreign Ministry.

## Key Points
- The talks mark the 25th round of diplomatic discussions on boundary issues between China and India.
- The discussions involve special representatives from both countries, indicating high-level engagement.
- The meeting is set to take place in Beijing, highlighting the location's significance.
- The announcement was made by the Chinese Foreign Ministry, underscoring official confirmation.


